 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5515+) **Merged** the **old split/interdependent Foreign Advisor** implementation from the two-file setup (`CvForeignAdvisor.py` + `CvExoticForeignAdvisor.py`) into a **single unified** [CvForeignAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvForeignAdvisor.py) with the **full tab set** (as of now Relations/Glance/Active/Bonus/Info/Tech/Cities). In our findings, **this was the only screen file** using that **interdependent split** pattern, so merging it into one file directly **fixes that inconsistency** and **reduces maintenance burden**; other major screen files such as [CvMainInterface.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMainInterface.py) and [CvInfoScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvInfoScreen.py) are lengthy but unified files. By contrast, true alternatives use independent variants (for example BUG/non-BUG [CvBUGMilitaryAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvBUGMilitaryAdvisor.py) / [CvMilitaryAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMilitaryAdvisor.py) paths), not interdependent split files.
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5516+) **Remove screen-dependent geometry computation** from `__init__` in advisors because this advisor object is created before a reliable screen context exists; doing layout in `interfaceScreen` **ensures correct values for the current resolution**. Keeping **only screen-independent edge constants** in `__init__` ensures **no redundant recomputation** is made again in `interfaceScreen`, and **catches loud screen-dependent errors** in `__init__`.
 - **Heavily refactor and simplify Sevopedia Main** so it is much easier to add, reorder, or modify or otherwise maintain categories. See [Sevopedia reworks (example 0.0)](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Sevopedia_Reworks.md#example-00-heavily-refactored-sevopedia-maintain-so-it-is-much-easier-to-maintain-or-customize).
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5789+) **Collapse multiline statements to single-line form** (e.g., `draw_expandable_text_panel(screen, self.top, szTitle, self.X_HISTORY, self.Y_HISTORY, self.W_HISTORY, self.H_HISTORY, szText, self.bHistoryExpanded, self.top.SAS_PEDIA_PYTHON_HISTORY_EXPAND)`): much **easier** to **scan**, **maintain**, and **grep**, especially **for LLMs**. Often done using scripts to batch process it, and done as we go rather than all at once since this is a recent change. Especially important in [CvMainInterface.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMainInterface.py) where ~2158 lines of code have been collapsed to ~879 lines. See also [LLM_Helpers (README.md)](/LLM_Helpers/README.md) and [PR#23](https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/pull/23).
 - Convert **single quote to double quote** (e.g. `'BONUS_IRON'` to `"BONUS_IRON"`), which allowed to **detect and fix incorrect fields** and later strengthen them with `getInfoTypeOrFail(...)`.
 - **Performance & code cleanup:** Broad Python/XML/C++ optimizations (e.g., removed giant ConfigObj docstring (see [KI#21.5](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#215---addressed--fixed---removed-the-giant-configobj-docstring-very-inefficiently-in-the-python-code-and-commented-out-most-if-not-all-as-well)); cached hot values via `static const`/hoisting; normalized inconsistent asset names (see for example [KI#18](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#18---very-inconsistent-naming-in-some-assets))), **map-type heaviness caching** (`CvGame::recomputeMapnameHeaviness`) so land/naval checks run once per game (feeds UNITAI tuning) (see [KI#42](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#42---enhancedaddressed-tune-ais-preferred-based-unitai-based-on-war-status-offense-mode-defense-mode-combined-power-ratios-of-ennemies-etc-if-any-other-general-sanity-checks-and-efficiency-city-size-map-type-land-heavy-vs-water-heavy-vs-other-if-any-for-example-general-suicide-or-such-tendencies-etc), **bonus-specific builds/improvements caching** (e.g. `CvUnitAI::getBonusSpecificLandBuilds`), [AI Personality Panel performance optimization notes](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_AI_Personality_Panel.md#notes-about-performance-optimization-of-the-ai-personality-panel-caching)), **feature-level caching** (AI Personality Panel), refactor **extremely redundant code** (e.g. `refreshUnitSelection` in [CvMilitaryAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMilitaryAdvisor.py)), cache redundant computation (e.g. **store per turn and player** top cities' values `CvCityAI::AI_buildingValue`), etc.
